id: pm-1j5j21
title: "GH-921/GH-922: merge-decision receipts are not durable in fresh-clone CI"
description: "Pending merge-decision receipts live only in clone-local ignored state, so a fresh checkout cannot distinguish a lossy concurrent merge; history-repair can erase the last tracked drift signal and make discarded work pass strict health."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-07T08:33:38.852Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-08T15:39:03.748Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Merge-decision receipts required by validation survive a fresh clone and clean CI checkout without relying on ignored local files; the field-aware merge driver and health/validate surfaces agree on durable evidence; isolated two-branch merge tests cover both lossless and discarded-value decisions and keep history hash validation intact
parent: pm-doxj
risk: critical
confidence: high
severity: critical
expected_result: "Discarded-value provenance and acknowledgment are durable, pushed, and enforceable from a fresh clone before repair can make the workspace green."
actual_result: "The merge-performing clone sees a pending decision, but a fresh clone loses it; after history-repair, strict health can pass a commit that discarded a peer edit."
affected_version: 2026.8.6
component: merge safety and durable history
